      "description": "The Faculty | Kalamazoo College – Academics Skip to main content About K K-Plan Academics Admission Alumni GIVE News Life at K Athletics APPLY Close Navigation Academics Home » Academics » The Faculty Areas of Study The Faculty GLCA Programs Honors, Awards and Prizes Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Course Schedule The Faculty Kalamazoo College’s faculty of nationally and internationally respected scholars bring deep expertise and a passion for teaching to their classrooms and labs. They are dedicated to developing the strengths of every student, preparing them for lifelong learning, career readiness, intercultural understanding, social responsibility, and leadership. 10:1 student-to-faculty ratio 106 full-time faculty members 97 percent of full-time faculty hold a Ph.D. or terminal degree 79 percent of faculty are tenured/tenure-track 53 percent of faculty are women K is committed to building a talented and diverse faculty that reflects our student body and the world around us. At Kalamazoo College, teaching and mentorship goes beyond the classroom to include working together on research projects, college committees, and community projects. The connections students and faculty form often last well beyond graduation. Faculty News New Tenure-Track Faculty Bring Neuroscience, Art, Fresh Perspectives Student-Athlete, Researcher Runs Toward Cleaner Air In Athletics and the Lab, Resilience is a Part of the Game One Lab, Three Student-Athletes and Some Tiny Worms From Mentor to Memoirist: Ahmed Hussen’s ‘The Dessie Kid’ Alphabetical List of Faculty Apps, Hannah (Economics and Business) Title Thomas K. Kreilick Professor of Economics and Business Department of Economics and Business Office DEWING 301 Office Phone 269.337.7024 E-mail happs@kzoo.edu Web Page http://econbusn.kzoo.edu/people/faculty-staff/#Apps Education A.B.  University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill Ph.D. University of Pennsylvania Arias-Rotondo, Daniela (Chemistry) Title Roger F. a